      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What are the most common VOCs in manufacturing facilities?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The most prevalent VOCs include toluene, xylene, acetone, methyl ethyl ketone (MEK), formaldehyde, benzene, and isopropanol. Paint and coating operations typically emit aromatic hydrocarbons (toluene, xylene), while pharmaceutical and chemical plants release a broader range including chlorinated solvents, alcohols, and ketones. The specific VOCs depend on your raw materials and processes."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much does VOC control equipment cost for a small-to-medium facility?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Capital costs vary widely based on air flow rate and VOC concentration. For a small facility (5,000–10,000 m³/hr), expect 25–75 lakhs rupees for basic carbon adsorption systems, 50 lakhs–1.5 crores for thermal oxidizers, and 75 lakhs–2 crores for catalytic systems. Operating costs range from 5 to 40 rupees per 1,000 m³ treated. Solvent recovery systems often achieve 2–4 year payback through recovered material value."
      }
