        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Penalties escalate based on violation severity and history. First-time violations typically result in notices requiring corrective action within 30–90 days. Continued non-compliance leads to Consent to Operate suspension, fines up to 1,00,000 rupees under the Air Act, potential imprisonment up to 5 years for repeat offenses, and civil liability for health damages and public liability under environmental damage laws."
      }
